# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Task Studio PWA — environment
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed variables reach the browser, and every one of them is
# INLINED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time rather than read at runtime. So this
# file is public by construction: never put a secret in it, and understand that
# changing a value here has no effect on an already-built app. See the note in
# src/shared/config/env.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The NestJS API, including the version prefix.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3333/api/v1

# The Socket.io origin: the same host WITHOUT the /api/v1 path. Socket.io
# connects to an origin, not to a REST route, and pointing it at the prefixed
# URL is the mistake that produces a permanently grey "Live" pill with a 404 in
# the network tab.
VITE_SOCKET_URL=http://localhost:3333

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT read from this file by the deployed app — Vercel inlines what
# is set in its own dashboard (Settings > Environment Variables), and the
# Docker image takes them as --build-arg. This block is here so the shape is
# written down in one place.
#
# Against the API on its own droplet:
#
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com/api/v1
#   VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://api.your-domain.com
#
# Both must be https. The app is served over TLS, and a browser refuses to let
# an https page open an ws:// socket or fetch an http:// URL — which surfaces
# as mixed-content errors rather than as anything naming the cause.
#
# After changing either on Vercel, REDEPLOY. Vercel does not rebuild on an
# environment change alone, so the old value stays in the bundle until it does.
